---
title: DndController API
description: Full API reference for DndController — reactive getters, event callbacks, methods, and types.
---

# DndController API

The `DndController` is the core engine that manages all drag-and-drop state and logic. You can create one explicitly or let `DndProvider` create one automatically.

## Constructor

```ts
import {
    DndController,
    PointerSensor,
    KeyboardSensor,
    centerPoint,
    overlap,
    restrictToVerticalAxis,
    defaultAnnouncements,
} from '@horuse/svelte-dnd';

// Minimal — all options have sensible defaults
const controller = new DndController();

// Full config:
const controller = new DndController({
    scroll: {
        scrollZoneRatio: 0.2, // trigger zone = 20% of container height/width (default: 0.3)
        maxSpeed: 20,          // max px/frame at 60fps (default: 30)
        stopOnDrop: true,      // stop scroll immediately on drop (default: false — scroll continues during ghost animation)
    },
    preview: {
        showDelay: 150,     // ms before preview slot appears (default: 300)
        collapseDelay: 400, // ms before slot collapses — match --dnd-preview-duration-out (default: 200)
    },
    debug: true,                             // position validation warnings in console
    sensors: [new PointerSensor(), new KeyboardSensor()], // see /docs/sensors
    collision: overlap({ threshold: '25%' }), // see /docs/collision
    modifiers: [restrictToVerticalAxis],      // see /docs/modifiers
    announcements: {                          // see /docs/accessibility
        ...defaultAnnouncements,
        onDragStart: ({ item }) => `Picked up ${item.id}.`,
    },
    strategies: [],                          // custom container strategies, see /docs/custom-strategies
});

// Default values (what you get when omitting each option):
const controller = new DndController({
    scroll: {
        scrollZoneRatio: 0.3,
        maxSpeed: 30,
        stopOnDrop: false,
    },
    preview: {
        showDelay: 300,
        collapseDelay: 200,
    },
    debug: false,
    sensors: [new PointerSensor(), new KeyboardSensor()],
    collision: centerPoint,  // ghost center must be inside zone rect
    modifiers: [],
    announcements: {
        onDragStart: ({ item }) => `Started dragging item ${item.id}.`,
        onDragOver: ({ item, current }) => `Item ${item.id} is over ${current.id} at position ${current.position}.`,
        onDrop: ({ item, target }) => `Dropped item ${item.id} into ${target.id} at position ${target.position}.`,
        onCancel: ({ item }) => `Dragging ${item.id} was cancelled.`,
    },
    strategies: [], // built-in 'sortable' and 'target' are always registered
});
```

Pass it to the provider via the `controller` prop:

```svelte
<DndProvider {controller}>
    <!-- your DnD content -->
</DndProvider>
```

This gives you direct access to the controller's methods and reactive getters.

## Reactive Getters

All getters are Svelte 5 reactive (`$state` / `$derived` internally).

| Getter | Type | Description |
|--------|------|-------------|
| `dragging` | `boolean` | Whether a drag is currently in progress |
| `element` | `HTMLElement \| null` | The DOM element being dragged |
| `transform` | `{ x: number; y: number } \| null` | Current ghost position |
| `draggedItem` | `string \| null` | ID of the item being dragged |
| `draggedType` | `string \| null` | Type of the dragged item (from the `type` prop on `DndDraggable`) |
| `draggedItemData` | `Record<string, unknown> \| undefined` | Data attached to the dragged item |
| `size` | `{ width: number; height: number } \| null` | Size of the dragged element |
| `animatingReturn` | `boolean` | Whether the ghost is animating back to origin |
| `dropPreview` | `DropPreview \| null` | Current drop preview state |
| `dropZones` | `DropZone[]` | All registered drop zones |
| `filteredDropZones` | `DropZone[]` | Drop zones filtered by the dragged item's type |
| `debugZones` | `boolean` | Whether debug zone visualization is enabled |
| `performingDrop` | `boolean` | Whether a drop animation is in progress |
| `skipDropPreviewAnimation` | `boolean` | Whether preview animations are skipped |
| `dragSource` | `DragSource` | `'user'` during a real drag, `'programmatic'` during a simulation |

## Event Callbacks

All event methods return an unsubscribe function.

### onDragStart

```ts
const unsubscribe = controller.onDragStart(({ item, source }) => {
    console.log('Started dragging:', item.id, 'from', source.id, 'at position', source.position);
});

// Later: unsubscribe()
```

### onDragEnd

Fired when a drag ends — regardless of whether it was dropped or cancelled.

```ts
controller.onDragEnd(({ item, source, target, cancelled }) => {
    if (cancelled) {
        console.log(item.id, 'returned to', source.id);
    } else {
        console.log(item.id, 'moved to', target?.id);
    }
});
```

### onDropCancelled

Fired when a drag is cancelled — the ghost returns to origin and no drop occurred. Use this to distinguish a cancel from a successful drop.

```ts
controller.onDropCancelled(({ item, source }) => {
    console.log('Drag cancelled:', item.id, 'back to', source.id);
});
```

### onDrop

The main callback for handling item reordering or moving between containers. `DndController` is generic — the `TData` type parameter narrows `item.data` in `onDrop`.

```ts
interface TaskData { label: string; priority: number }

const controller = new DndController<TaskData>()

controller.onDrop(({ item, source, target }) => {
    // item.id:          ID of the dragged item
    // item.data:        TaskData | undefined  ← typed!
    // source.id:        container the item came from
    // source.position:  original position in source container
    // target.id:        container where item was dropped
    // target.position:  insertion index in target container
});
```

### onDragOver

Fired each time the drag-over target (container + position) changes. Useful for highlighting the active drop zone in custom UIs.

```ts
controller.onDragOver(({ item, current, previous }) => {
    console.log(item.id, 'moved to', current.id, 'position', current.position);
    if (previous) console.log('was over', previous.id);
});
```

### onZonesInvalidated

```ts
controller.onZonesInvalidated(() => {
    // fired after auto-scroll moves a container,
    // invalidating existing drop zone coordinates
});
```

Subscribe to recalculate zones if you manage them manually.

## Methods

### updateTransform

```ts
controller.updateTransform(transform: { x: number; y: number }): void
```

Updates the ghost element position during drag.

### updateMousePosition

```ts
controller.updateMousePosition(mouseX: number, mouseY: number): void
```

Updates the mouse position for drop zone detection and auto-scroll.

### performDrop

```ts
controller.performDrop(
    sourceId: string,
    sourceData: Record<string, unknown> | undefined,
    targetContainerId: string,
    position: number
): void
```

Performs a drop with animation to the target zone.

### endDrag

```ts
controller.endDrag(shouldAnimate?: boolean): void
```

Ends the drag. When `shouldAnimate` is `true` (default), the ghost animates back to its origin.

### setPreviewConfig

```ts
controller.setPreviewConfig(config: PreviewConfig): void
```

Updates preview animation delays at runtime.

```ts
controller.setPreviewConfig({ showDelay: 150, collapseDelay: 400 });
```

> **Note:** `collapseDelay` should match your `--dnd-preview-duration-out` CSS variable so the slot collapses only after the CSS transition finishes.

### setSkipDropPreviewAnimation

```ts
controller.setSkipDropPreviewAnimation(value: boolean): void
```

Controls whether `DndPreview` open/close animations are skipped. Useful when you need previews to appear or disappear instantly (e.g. during rapid container switches).

### toggleDebugZones

```ts
controller.toggleDebugZones(): void
```

Toggles visual overlay of all drop zones. Useful for development and debugging.

### destroy

```ts
controller.destroy(): void
```

Cleans up all internal state, listeners, and registries. Called automatically when `DndProvider` unmounts (if it created the controller).

## Programmatic Animations

For running animations without user interaction see the [Simulations](/docs/simulations) page. The controller exposes `simulateReturn()` and `simulateDrop()` as thin delegates to `DndSimulator`.

## Types

All types below are exported from `@horuse/svelte-dnd`.

```ts
interface DropZone {
    containerId: string;
    position: number;
    direction: DndDirection;
    itemId?: string;
    rect: { x: number; y: number; width: number; height: number };
}

interface ScrollConfig {
    /** Fraction of container size that triggers auto-scroll. Default: 0.3 */
    scrollZoneRatio?: number;
    /** Maximum scroll speed in px/frame at 60fps. Default: 30 */
    maxSpeed?: number;
    /** Stop auto-scroll immediately when drop is committed. Default: false — scroll continues during ghost animation for a smoother feel. */
    stopOnDrop?: boolean;
}

interface PreviewConfig {
    /** Debounce delay (ms) before revealing the preview slot. Default: 300 */
    showDelay?: number;
    /** Delay (ms) before collapsing the slot — should match --dnd-preview-duration-out. Default: 200 */
    collapseDelay?: number;
}

interface DndControllerConfig {
    scroll?: ScrollConfig;
    preview?: PreviewConfig;
    /** Enable dev warnings (unknown strategy mode, etc.). Default: false */
    debug?: boolean;
    strategies?: (ContainerStrategy | StrategyFactory)[];
    /** Active input sensors. Defaults to [PointerSensor, KeyboardSensor]. See [Sensors](/docs/sensors) */
    sensors?: SensorDescriptor[];
    /** Global collision algorithm. Per-container `collision` prop takes priority. See [Collision Detection](/docs/collision) */
    collision?: CollisionAlgorithm;
    /** Transform modifiers applied to ghost position on every move. See [Modifiers](/docs/modifiers) */
    modifiers?: Modifier[];
    /** Screen-reader announcement strings. See [Accessibility](/docs/accessibility) */
    announcements?: Announcements;
}

type StrategyFactory = (state: DndState) => ContainerStrategy;

// Rich event objects passed to all callbacks:
interface DndItemInfo<TData = Record<string, unknown>> {
    id: string;
    data: TData | undefined;
    type: string | undefined;
    element: HTMLElement;
}
interface DndContainerInfo {
    id: string;
    droppable: Droppable;
    position: number;
}
interface DragStartEvent     { item: DndItemInfo; source: DndContainerInfo }
interface DragEndEvent       { item: DndItemInfo; source: DndContainerInfo; target: DndContainerInfo | null; cancelled: boolean }
interface DropEvent<TData>   { item: DndItemInfo<TData>; source: DndContainerInfo; target: DndContainerInfo }
interface DragOverEvent      { item: DndItemInfo; source: DndContainerInfo; current: DndContainerInfo; previous: DndContainerInfo | null }
interface DropCancelledEvent { item: DndItemInfo; source: DndContainerInfo }

type DragStartCallback    = (event: DragStartEvent) => void;
type DragEndCallback      = (event: DragEndEvent) => void;
type DropCancelledCallback = (event: DropCancelledEvent) => void;
type DropCallback<TData = Record<string, unknown>> = (event: DropEvent<TData>) => void;
type DragOverCallback     = (event: DragOverEvent) => void;
type DndDirection = 'vertical' | 'horizontal' | 'grid';
type DndMode = 'sortable' | 'target' | (string & {}); // custom modes allowed
type DragSource = 'user' | 'programmatic';
```

For custom drop zone strategies see [Custom Strategies](/docs/custom-strategies).
